\textbf{Senior Manager, Forward Deployed Engineering} \hfill \textit{Jul 2026 – present}
\vspace{\topsep} % Vertical space between sections
\begin{tightemize}
    \item Implemented pre/post-sales life cycle processes for customers deploying AI inference clusters across 7+ teams and 5 geographies. Built agentic system using LangGraph to coordinate delivery and compute resource scheduling for demo, proof of concept, and production deployments. 
    
    \item Architected customer kubernetes clusters for AI inference serving and development using tt-operator, ansible, helm, and \href{https://docs.tenstorrent.com/cloud-native-support/}{\texttt{cloud native tooling}}.
\end{tightemize}

\textbf{Senior Staff Engineer, Field Applications - Machine Learning} \hfill \textit{Sep 2024 – Jul 2026}
\begin{tightemize}
    \item \href{https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-inference-server}{\texttt{tt-inference-server}}: co-led cross-functional team of 20+ engineers delivering tt-inference-server, an open-source inference server deployment and benchmarking framework for Tenstorrent AI accelerators.

    \item Designed CI test and release system for inference serving stack with automated regression detection. 18 releases completed, 60+ AI models supported (27 LLMs/VLMs) across 9 different hardware configurations.
    
    \item Partnered with enterprise customers to define AI system requirements for agentic application integration with Tenstorrent hardware. Customer-specific optimization of LLM inference for latency/throughput/cost via hardware configuration, batch size, parallelism.
\end{tightemize}

\textbf{Staff Engineer, Field Applications - Machine Learning} \hfill \textit{Apr 2023 – Sep 2024}
\begin{tightemize}
    \item Prototyped cloud deployments of vLLM with LLMs running on Tenstorrent ASICs. using Docker, AWS EKS, ELB, Azure API Gateway, and Terraform.

    \item \href{https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-studio}{\texttt{tt-studio}}: Built backend for open-source customer reference AI applications using Docker, Django, LangChain and self-hosting LLM inference APIs.

    \item \href{https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-buda-benchmarks}{\texttt{tt-buda-benchmarks}}: benchmarking and evaluations for LLM and CNN models to track model performance and accuracy across AI compiler releases.
\end{tightemize}
